{"title": "Bump plugin.json to 0.13.0 with a matching CHANGELOG heading", "files": [".claude-plugin/plugin.json (the \"version\" field)", "CHANGELOG.md (prepend the newest heading)"], "testCycle": "`python3 scripts/validate_plugin.py; echo rc=$?` ends `rc=0`. Run the release gate (find it with `ls scripts/release_gate*`, then `python3` that file) and it exits 0. `grep -m1 '^## \\[' CHANGELOG.md` prints `## [0.13.0]`. Run `bash tests/test-scripts.sh` alone and it shows `0 failed`.", "specExcerpt": "4. Bump plugin.json to 0.13.0 and add the matching CHANGELOG heading.\nCLAUDE.md: `plugin.json` `version` \u2014 add the matching `## [x.y.z]` as the newest heading in `CHANGELOG.md`, same commit (the release gate fails otherwise).", "steps": ["Red first: change only `.claude-plugin/plugin.json` \"version\" to \"0.13.0\" and run the release gate. It must FAIL because the changelog heading is missing. Record that output.", "Prepend `## [0.13.0]` above the current newest heading in CHANGELOG.md, copying the date format of the heading below it. Add 3 bullets: the decision that ownership stays in the filename, with the rejected body field and a pointer to the DECISIONS.md id; the four new sentinel-ownership cases; and the FLOOR_SHELL raise. State plainly that no runtime behaviour changed.", "Run the release gate and `python3 scripts/validate_plugin.py`. Both must exit 0. Then run `shellcheck` on any .sh file you touched (none are expected) and the shell suite alone.", "Run `git add .claude-plugin/plugin.json CHANGELOG.md && git commit -m 'v0.13.0: sentinel ownership stays in the filename (decision + pins)'`. Push with `git push -u origin chore/sentinel-ownership-decision`; never a bare push."]}
